## useEffect Dependency Array

```tsx
// Runs after EVERY render
useEffect(() => { console.log('render'); });

// Runs ONCE after initial render (componentDidMount)
useEffect(() => {
  fetchData();
}, []);

// Runs when userId changes (componentDidUpdate)
useEffect(() => {
  fetchUser(userId);
}, [userId]);
```

## Fetching on Mount

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  let cancelled = false;

  async function load() {
    const data = await fetchPosts();
    if (!cancelled) setPosts(data);
  }

  load();

  // Cleanup — prevent setState on unmounted component
  return () => { cancelled = true; };
}, []);
```

## React StrictMode Double Invocation

In development with StrictMode, React 18 intentionally runs effects **twice** (mount → unmount → mount) to surface missing cleanup functions. This only happens in development — production runs once.

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const sub = subscribe(id);
  return () => sub.unsubscribe(); // cleanup is required
}, [id]);
```

## ESLint Rule

The `react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` ESLint rule warns when dependencies are missing. Never silence it by adding `// eslint-disable` — fix the actual dependency or restructure the logic.

